From 41c45f378e8f433b56c4da9b80edcdfd67fcebfb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Porkchop Express <51079966+misteraddons@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 9 Sep 2026 03:32:35 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 1/1] HID: google-stadiaff: bind Classic2USB and RetroZord for force feedback

Add Classic2USB (Reflex Adapt, 16d0:1460) and RetroZord (1209:595a) to
the existing Google Stadia force-feedback driver's device table using
HID_GROUP_GENERIC. Both use the existing Stadia rumble output report
in compatible firmware, so no other driver code changes are needed --
this is purely two additional rows in stadia_devices[].

CONFIG_HID_GOOGLE_STADIA_FF=y is already on in our linux.config; the
driver is already built, and these two IDs are the entire gap.

Without this, both adapters are unclaimed by any specialised driver
and fall through to hid-generic's catch-all match
(HID_DEVICE(HID_BUS_ANY, HID_GROUP_ANY, HID_ANY_ID, HID_ANY_ID),
drivers/hid/hid-generic.c). They still enumerate and work as plain
input devices -- buttons and axes come through hidinput regardless of
which driver binds -- but EV_FF/FF_RUMBLE is never registered, so
force feedback silently does nothing on either adapter. No probe
error is logged, because hid-generic's probe succeeds; the failure is
purely a missing capability on an otherwise-working device.

Main_MiSTer coupling. input.cpp special-cases exactly these two
VID:PID pairs at several sites, independent of this patch but load-
bearing for why the adapters must bind a real driver rather than
hid-generic:
  - input.cpp:52-53, the Reflex Adapt / RetroZord predicate:
    `(vid == 0x16D0 && (pid == 0x127E || pid == 0x1460)) // Reflex Adapt
     || (vid == 0x1209 && pid == 0x595A); // RetroZord`
  - input.cpp:4176-4177, make_unique() dedup:
    `make_unique(0x16D0, 0x1460, 1);  // Reflex Adapt Classic2USB`
    `make_unique(0x1209, 0x595A, 1);  // RetroZord adapter`
  - input.cpp:5102 and :5349, NeGcon/Guncon emulation match on
    `input[i].vid == 0x1209 && input[i].pid == 0x595A` together with
    `strstr(input[i].name, "RZordPsWheel")` / `strstr(uniq, "RZordPsGun")`.
  - input.cpp:5496, RetroZord UNIQ-field mode differentiation re-checks
    the same 0x16D0/0x1460 and 0x1209/0x595A pairs alongside
    `strlen(uniq)`.
None of those name/uniq matches change with this patch: stadia_probe()
(drivers/hid/hid-google-stadiaff.c) calls
`hid_hw_start(hdev, HID_CONNECT_DEFAULT & ~HID_CONNECT_FF)` -- it only
masks off HID_CONNECT_FF (it wires its own memless FF instead of the
generic hidinput FF path) and never writes hdev->name, hdev->uniq, or
hidinput->input->name/->uniq itself; those strings come from hid-core's
generic USB-descriptor connect path before any per-driver .probe runs,
so binding stadiaff instead of hid-generic changes nothing Main_MiSTer
matches on.

